    <symbol id="i-partner" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M3 16.8c4.1.1 4.2-8.6 9-9.5 3.5-.7 5.1 2.1 9 2.1-2 1.1-3.2 3.2-5.7 3.5-2 .2-3.1-.8-4.7-.5-2.4.5-3.2 4.7-7.6 4.4Z" fill="currentColor"/><path d="M6.1 19.7c3.5-.1 4.6-3.2 7.3-3.5 1.3-.2 2.5.2 4.1-.1-2.2 1.7-4.2 3.4-7.4 3.7-1.5.1-2.8.1-4-.1Z" fill="currentColor" opacity=".72"/></symbol>
  </svg>

  <% if (page === "landing") { %>
    <main class="landing-page">
      <header class="landing-header">
        <a class="landing-brand" href="/"><img src="/images/chirpy.png" alt="Chirpy" /><span>CHIRPY</span></a>
        <nav class="landing-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
          <a href="#community">Community</a>
          <a href="/terms">Terms</a>
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
          <a href="/login" class="landing-signin">Sign in</a>
        </nav>
      </header>
      <section class="landing-hero" id="community">
        <div class="landing-logo"><img src="/images/chirpy.png" alt="Chirpy" /></div>
        <p class="landing-kicker">A community built around you</p>
        <h1 class="landing-title">Find your people.<br /><span>Start the conversation.</span></h1>
        <p class="landing-description">A place to share what matters, discover new perspectives, and keep up with the conversations that bring us together.</p>
        <a class="landing-cta" href="/auth/discord">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M19.7 5.2a18.2 18.2 0 0 0-4.5-1.4l-.6 1.2a16.8 16.8 0 0 0-5.2 0l-.6-1.2a18.2 18.2 0 0 0-4.5 1.4C1.5 9.4.7 13.5 1.1 17.5a18.3 18.3 0 0 0 5.5 2.8l1.2-1.9-1.9-.9.5-.4a13 13 0 0 0 11.2 0l.5.4-1.9.9 1.2 1.9a18.3 18.3 0 0 0 5.5-2.8c.5-4.6-.8-8.7-3.2-12.3ZM8.7 14.8c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2s.9-2 2-2 2 .9 2 2-.9 2-2 2Zm6.6 0c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2s.9-2 2-2 2 .9 2 2-.9 2-2 2Z"/></svg>
          Continue with Discord
        </a>
        <p class="landing-footnote">Your community is waiting.</p>
        <nav class="landing-legal-links" aria-label="Legal information"><a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a></nav>
      </section>
    </main>

  <% } else if (page === "terms" || page === "privacy") { %>
    <main class="legal-page">
      <header class="legal-header">
        <a class="legal-brand" href="/"><img src="/images/chirpy.png" alt="Chirpy" /><span>CHIRPY</span></a>
        <nav class="legal-nav" aria-label="Legal navigation"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="/terms">Terms</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a></nav>
      </header>
      <% if (page === "terms") { %>
        <article class="legal-content">
          <p class="eyebrow">Chirpy · Service terms</p>
          <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
          <p class="legal-intro">These terms explain the rules for using Chirpy, a community service with Discord sign-in, profiles, posts, images, messages, notifications, and polls. By accessing Chirpy, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use the service.</p>
          <section><h2>1. Eligibility and your account</h2><p>Chirpy is intended for people who are at least 13 years old in the United States. You may not use Chirpy if you are under 13. If you are 13 or older but have not reached the age of majority where you live, you may use Chirpy only with the involvement and permission of a parent or legal guardian. You must also meet Discord’s applicable minimum-age requirements and follow Discord’s terms. You are responsible for activity under your account and for keeping access to your Discord account secure. Sign-in is provided by Discord; Chirpy does not receive or store your Discord password.</p></section>
          <section><h2>2. Community content and conduct</h2><p>You are responsible for content you submit, including profile details, posts, uploaded images, comments, messages, mentions, and poll questions or options. You must have the rights and permissions needed to submit it. Do not use Chirpy to break the law, threaten or harass people, share another person’s private information without permission, impersonate others, distribute malware, infringe intellectual-property rights, or interfere with the service. Do not attempt to bypass access controls or misuse the service.</p></section>
          <section><h2>3. Your content and permission to operate Chirpy</h2><p>You retain any rights you have in your content. You give Chirpy a limited, non-exclusive permission to host, store, reproduce, and display content as needed to provide and maintain the features you use, including showing posts and images to other users, storing messages and poll votes, and displaying social activity notifications. This permission ends when the content is removed from active service, subject to copies retained as described in the Privacy Policy and technical backups or records.</p></section>
          <section><h2>4. Moderation and account restrictions</h2><p>Chirpy staff may review content and accounts, remove or hide posts, mute accounts, change access, or terminate accounts when reasonably needed to enforce these terms, respond to safety concerns, or protect the service. Moderation decisions may be made with or without advance notice where permitted by law. Terminated accounts lose access. A terminated account may be appealed once within 30 days; after that period it cannot be reinstated and account content is scheduled for purge, subject to minimal reservation and moderation records described in the Privacy Policy.</p></section>
          <section><h2>5. Intellectual property and reports</h2><p>Chirpy’s name, logo, interface, and original service materials are owned by or licensed to the service operator and are protected by applicable law. These terms do not grant you ownership of them. If you believe content on Chirpy infringes your rights, contact the service operator using the contact information described below with enough detail to identify the content and your concern. No designated notice agent or legal contact has been configured yet.</p></section>
          <section><h2>6. Third-party services and availability</h2><p>Chirpy depends on third parties, including Discord for authentication and the MongoDB service configured by the operator for application data. Those services have their own terms, privacy practices, availability, and security controls. Chirpy may be changed, interrupted, or discontinued. Features are provided as available, and the operator does not promise uninterrupted service, error-free operation, or permanent availability of content.</p></section>
          <section><h2>7. Disclaimers and liability</h2><p>To the fullest extent allowed by law, Chirpy is provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of any kind, whether express, implied, or statutory, including implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. To the fullest extent allowed by law, the operator will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages, or for loss of data, profits, goodwill, or service access, arising from use of Chirpy. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot legally be limited or excludes rights that cannot legally be waived.</p></section>
          <section><h2>8. Changes and governing rules</h2><p>These terms may be updated as Chirpy changes or legal requirements evolve. The current version will be posted at this URL; continued use after an update takes effect means you accept the revised terms. These terms are intended to be governed by applicable United States law and, where applicable, the laws of the state in which the service operator is established, without displacing mandatory consumer protections that apply to you.</p></section>
          <div class="legal-contact-note"><strong>Operator contact:</strong> Site operator contact information has not been supplied or configured. It must be added before production use so users can submit legal, safety, or account requests. These terms are general service information, not legal advice.</div>
        </article>
      <% } else { %>
        <article class="legal-content">
          <p class="eyebrow">Chirpy · Your information</p>
          <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
          <p class="legal-intro">This policy describes information handled by Chirpy, how it is used, and choices currently available. It applies to the Chirpy website and its posts, profiles, images, internal messages, polls, mention notifications, and moderation features.</p>
          <section><h2>1. Who operates Chirpy</h2><p>The service operator has not supplied a legal business name, mailing address, or privacy contact. This page does not invent one. “Chirpy” below means the operator of this application. Operator contact information must be configured and published before production so people can direct privacy or safety requests to a responsible contact.</p></section>
          <section><h2>2. Information the service handles</h2><ul><li><strong>Discord sign-in and profile:</strong> Discord account ID, username, display name, and avatar details returned by Discord’s identity sign-in. The app uses these to create and maintain your Chirpy account and profile.</li><li><strong>Content and activity:</strong> your Chirpy handle, display name, bio, posts, uploaded image bytes, comments, internal messages, likes, reposts, bookmarks, poll questions/options and votes, and social notification records for follows, mentions, comments, likes, reposts, and messages.</li><li><strong>Safety and service records:</strong> staff role, verification application and decision status, mute or termination status, and moderation audit records needed to administer the service.</li><li><strong>Technical data:</strong> the app uses an HttpOnly session cookie and stores session records and short-lived OAuth state in MongoDB. The sign-in cookie has a rolling 30-day inactivity expiration and is removed on sign-out. The hosting platform or network providers may generate technical or request logs according to their own settings; the operator has not configured a public log-retention statement.</li></ul></section>
          <section><h2>3. How information is used</h2><p>Information is used to authenticate users, operate accounts and profiles, display community content, save messages and interactions, record poll votes, administer moderation and verification, protect service integrity, and respond to operational or legal needs. Discord profile images may be loaded from Discord’s content-delivery network. The application code contains no advertising or analytics feature, but third-party hosting and infrastructure may process technical data under their own terms.</p></section>
          <section><h2>4. Storage, sharing, and service providers</h2><p>Application records, including account data, user content, image bytes, messages, polls, notifications, and moderation records, are stored in the MongoDB database configured by the operator. Discord handles the authentication flow and supplies identity data; the app does not store your Discord password or retain the OAuth access token after retrieving your identity. The app is hosted on infrastructure selected by the operator. The specific hosting provider, processing locations, and provider retention settings have not been identified on this site. Data may be processed by those providers to deliver their services or as required by law; their own privacy policies apply.</p><p>The app does not provide a public directory of recipients or a configured data-sale integration. Content you post or send may be visible to the recipients or users allowed by the feature and may be copied by people who can access it.</p></section>
          <section><h2>External resources</h2><p>The site loads typefaces from Google Fonts and may load Discord-hosted avatar images from Discord’s content-delivery network. Those providers may receive ordinary connection data, such as your IP address and browser request details, when your browser requests those resources.</p></section>
          <section><h2>5. Retention and deletion</h2><p>Account and content records are retained in the configured database while the account and service operate. The app currently has no self-service account deletion. A terminated account is disabled and may be reinstated only within 30 days of its current termination. After 30 days, Chirpy purges the account and associated posts, uploaded images, comments, poll votes, messages, notifications, follows, likes, reposts, and bookmarks from the application database. Purge runs periodically, so removal may not happen at the exact deadline.</p><p>To prevent a deleted identity or handle from being reused to evade a termination or claim the same handle, Chirpy retains a minimal tombstone containing the reserved normalized handle (if any), the account’s original database identifier, a keyed hash of its Discord ID, termination date, and one-time appeal-use/status and decision-reference metadata. The submitted appeal text and profile/content data are not copied into this tombstone. Moderation audit entries, which can include staff-entered action details such as mute or termination reasons, are retained with account-ID references. These minimal records are not a restored user account and cannot be used to sign in. MongoDB backups, if enabled, and provider logs may retain copies according to provider settings that are not specified here.</p><p>One appeal may be submitted within 30 days of a termination. Once used, an appeal is not available again even if an account is reinstated and later terminated. Appeals pending at the 30-day purge deadline are recorded as expired; staff cannot reinstate an account after the deadline.</p><p>You may request access, correction, or deletion by contacting the operator, but no contact details or request workflow are currently configured. Requests cannot be reliably processed until the operator publishes a contact method. Applicable legal requirements may affect what can be deleted or retained.</p></section>
          <section><h2>6. Security</h2><p>The service uses reasonable application measures such as Discord-based authentication, an HttpOnly session cookie, and server-side role checks. No online service or storage system can be guaranteed secure, and the operator cannot promise that unauthorized access, loss, or disclosure will never occur. Avoid sending highly sensitive information through Chirpy messages or posts.</p></section>
          <section><h2>7. Children and COPPA</h2><p>Chirpy is not intended for children under 13 in the United States, and the operator does not knowingly seek to collect personal information from a child under 13. If the operator learns that a child under 13 has provided personal information, the operator should take steps to delete it. A parent or guardian who believes a child’s information was submitted should contact the operator; contact details have not yet been configured and must be supplied before production. Users must also satisfy Discord’s applicable age requirements.</p></section>
          <section><h2>8. U.S. privacy rights and policy changes</h2><p>Depending on where you live, state privacy laws may provide rights concerning personal information, such as access, correction, deletion, or opting out of certain processing. The app does not currently implement an automated privacy-request portal. Contact the operator once contact information is published to submit a request; the operator will assess and respond as required by applicable law. This policy may change as the service or its providers change. The updated version will be posted at this URL.</p></section>
          <div class="legal-contact-note"><strong>Privacy contact:</strong> Site operator contact information has not been supplied or configured. This is an explicit operational gap, not a promise that a request portal or dedicated privacy officer exists. This policy is informational and is not legal advice.</div>
        </article>
      <% } %>
    </main>

  <% } else if (page === "maintenance") { %>
    <main class="maintenance-page">
      <div class="ambient-glow one" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="ambient-glow two" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="maintenance-dots top" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="maintenance-dots bottom" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <a class="maintenance-wordmark" href="/"><img src="/images/chirpy.png?v=1" alt="" /><span>CHIRPY</span></a>
      <div class="maintenance-status-top">Platform upgrades in progress</div>

      <section class="maintenance-card">
        <div class="maintenance-main">
          <div class="maintenance-brand">
            <div class="maintenance-logo"><img src="/images/chirpy.png?v=1" alt="Chirpy" /></div>
            <div class="maintenance-brand-copy"><p class="eyebrow">System notice</p><strong>CHIRPY</strong></div>
          </div>
          <p class="maintenance-kicker">A better experience is loading</p>
          <h1 class="maintenance-title">Under<br />Maintenance.</h1>
          <p class="maintenance-description">We’re refining Chirpy behind the scenes. The platform will return shortly with a cleaner, faster, and more polished experience.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="maintenance-side">
          <p class="maintenance-side-label">Current status</p>
          <div class="maintenance-status-box"><strong>Upgrade in progress</strong><p>Core services are temporarily unavailable while updates are applied.</p></div>
          <div class="maintenance-deployment"><span>Deployment</span><strong><%= maintenanceSettings.progress %>%</strong></div>
          <progress class="maintenance-progress" aria-label="Deployment progress" max="100" value="<%= maintenanceSettings.progress %>"><%= maintenanceSettings.progress %>%</progress>
          <button id="openAdmin" class="maintenance-admin" type="button">Admin access</button>
          <a class="maintenance-thanks" href="/login">Staff sign in with Discord</a>
          <div id="adminForm" hidden>
            <input id="adminPassword" class="maintenance-password" type="password" placeholder="Administrator password" autocomplete="current-password" />
            <p id="adminError" class="maintenance-error" aria-live="polite"></p>
            <button id="verifyAdmin" class="maintenance-admin" type="button">Continue</button>
          </div>
          <p class="maintenance-thanks">Thank you for your patience while we make Chirpy better.</p>
        </aside>
      </section>
    </main>
    <script>
      const openAdmin = document.getElementById("openAdmin");
      const adminForm = document.getElementById("adminForm");
      const passwordField = document.getElementById("adminPassword");
      const adminError = document.getElementById("adminError");
      const verifyButton = document.getElementById("verifyAdmin");

      openAdmin.addEventListener("click", () => {
        openAdmin.hidden = true;
        adminForm.hidden = false;
        passwordField.focus();
      });

      async function verifyAdmin() {
        adminError.textContent = "";
        verifyButton.disabled = true;
        verifyButton.textContent = "Checking…";
        try {
          const response = await fetch("/admin/verify", {
            method: "POST",
            headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
            body: JSON.stringify({ password: passwordField.value })
          });
          const result = await response.json();
          if (!response.ok) {
            adminError.textContent = result.message || "Could not verify password.";
            return;
          }
          window.location.href = result.redirect;
        } catch {
          adminError.textContent = "Can't reach the server. Check that it is running.";
        } finally {
          verifyButton.disabled = false;
          verifyButton.textContent = "Continue";
        }
      }

      verifyButton.addEventListener("click", verifyAdmin);
      passwordField.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
        if (event.key === "Enter") verifyAdmin();
      });
    </script>

  <% } else if (page === "terminated") { %>
    <main class="termination-page">
      <a class="termination-wordmark" href="/"><img src="/images/chirpy.png?v=1" alt="" /><span>CHIRPY</span></a>
      <section class="termination-card" aria-labelledby="terminationTitle">
        <div class="termination-icon" aria-hidden="true">!</div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Account status</p>
        <h1 id="terminationTitle">This account is terminated</h1>
        <p><%= safeTerminatedAccount.displayName %>, this Chirpy account is currently disabled and cannot access the app.</p>
        <% if (safeTerminatedAccount.reason || safeTerminatedAccount.terminatedAt) { %>
          <div class="termination-detail">
            <% if (safeTerminatedAccount.reason) { %><strong>Notice:</strong> <%= safeTerminatedAccount.reason %><br /><% } %>
            <% if (safeTerminatedAccount.terminatedAt) { %><strong>Effective:</strong> <time class="local-time" datetime="<%= new Date(safeTerminatedAccount.terminatedAt).toISOString() %>"><%= new Date(safeTerminatedAccount.terminatedAt).toISOString() %></time><% } %>
          </div>
        <% } %>
        <% if (safeAppealNotice) { %><p class="appeal-notice" role="status"><%= safeAppealNotice %></p><% } %>
        <section class="appeal-card" aria-labelledby="appealTitle">
          <h2 id="appealTitle">Termination appeal</h2>
          <% if (safeTerminatedAccount.appealStatus === "pending" && safeTerminatedAccount.appealEligible) { %>
            <p class="appeal-status">Your one-time appeal has been submitted and is awaiting staff review. It cannot be edited or submitted again.</p>
            <% if (safeTerminatedAccount.appealSubmittedAt) { %><p class="appeal-status">Submitted <time class="local-time" datetime="<%= new Date(safeTerminatedAccount.appealSubmittedAt).toISOString() %>"><%= new Date(safeTerminatedAccount.appealSubmittedAt).toISOString() %></time>.</p><% } %>
          <% } else if (safeTerminatedAccount.appealStatus === "pending") { %>
            <p class="appeal-status">Your one-time appeal was submitted but the 30-day period has passed. It can no longer result in reinstatement.</p>
          <% } else if (safeTerminatedAccount.appealUsed) { %>
            <p class="appeal-status"><% if (safeTerminatedAccount.appealStatus === "denied") { %>Your one-time appeal was denied. No further appeal can be submitted.<% } else if (safeTerminatedAccount.appealStatus === "accepted") { %>Your one-time appeal was accepted and the account was reinstated, but the account has since been terminated again. No further appeal can be submitted.<% } else if (safeTerminatedAccount.appealStatus === "expired") { %>Your one-time appeal expired at the end of the 30-day period. No further appeal can be submitted.<% } else { %>This account has already used its one-time appeal. No further appeal can be submitted.<% } %></p>
            <% if (safeTerminatedAccount.appealDecisionAt) { %><p class="appeal-status">Decision recorded <time class="local-time" datetime="<%= new Date(safeTerminatedAccount.appealDecisionAt).toISOString() %>"><%= new Date(safeTerminatedAccount.appealDecisionAt).toISOString() %></time>.</p><% } %>
          <% } else if (safeTerminatedAccount.appealEligible) { %>
            <p class="appeal-status">You may submit one appeal within 30 days of this termination. <span class="appeal-window">Time remaining: <span class="appeal-countdown" data-closes-at="<%= new Date(safeTerminatedAccount.appealClosesAt).toISOString() %>"></span></span></p>
            <p class="appeal-status">Your appeal is private and visible to Chirpy staff reviewing it. Do not include passwords, authentication codes, tokens, or other sensitive information.</p>
            <form method="POST" action="/account-terminated/appeal">
              <label for="appealText" class="muted">Explain why you believe this termination should be reviewed</label>
              <textarea id="appealText" name="appealText" minlength="20" maxlength="2000" required placeholder="Describe the relevant context (20–2,000 characters)."></textarea>
              <button type="submit">Submit one-time appeal</button>
            </form>
          <% } else { %>
            <p class="appeal-status">The 30-day appeal period has expired or no termination date is available. An appeal can no longer be submitted.</p>
          <% } %>
        </section>
        <div class="termination-actions">
          <a class="primary" href="/">Back to public home</a>
          <form method="POST" action="/logout"><button type="submit">Sign out</button></form>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <script>
      document.querySelectorAll(".local-time").forEach((element) => {
        const date = new Date(element.dateTime);
        if (Number.isFinite(date.getTime())) {
          element.textContent = new Intl.DateTimeFormat(undefined, {
            dateStyle: "medium",
            timeStyle: "short"
          }).format(date);
        }
      });
      document.querySelectorAll(".appeal-countdown").forEach((element) => {
        const closesAt = new Date(element.dataset.closesAt);
        const updateCountdown = () => {
          const remaining = closesAt.getTime() - Date.now();
          if (!Number.isFinite(remaining) || remaining <= 0) {
            element.textContent = "appeal period ended";
            return;
          }
          const totalMinutes = Math.ceil(remaining / 60000);
          const days = Math.floor(totalMinutes / 1440);
          const hours = Math.floor((totalMinutes % 1440) / 60);
          const minutes = totalMinutes % 60;
          element.textContent = [days ? `${days}d` : "", hours ? `${hours}h` : "", `${minutes}m`].filter(Boolean).join(" ");
        };
        updateCountdown();
        window.setInterval(updateCountdown, 60000);
      });
    </script>
  <% } else if (page === "error") { %>
    <main class="auth-page">
      <a class="auth-brand" href="/"><img src="/images/chirpy.png?v=1" alt="" /> CHIRPY</a>
      <section class="auth-card" role="alert">
        <div class="termination-icon" aria-hidden="true"><%= statusCode || "!" %></div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Chirpy · Request status</p>
        <h1><%= statusCode === 404 ? "Page not found" : statusCode === 403 ? "Request blocked" : "We couldn't complete that" %></h1>
        <p><%= statusMessage || "Please try again." %></p>
        <a class="auth-btn" href="/app">Return to Chirpy</a>
        <a class="back-home" href="/">Go to public home</a>
      </section>
    </main>

  <% } else if (page === "login") { %>
    <main class="auth-page">
      <a class="auth-brand" href="/"><img src="/images/chirpy.png?v=1" alt="" /> CHIRPY</a>
      <section class="auth-card">
        <div class="auth-logo"><img src="/images/chirpy.png?v=1" alt="Chirpy" /></div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Your Chirpy account</p>
        <h1>Sign in with Discord</h1>
        <p>Connect your Discord account to continue. New users choose a Chirpy handle after signing in.</p>
        <% if (error) { %><p class="form-error"><%= error %></p><% } %>
        <a class="auth-btn" href="/auth/discord?returnTo=<%= encodeURIComponent(returnTo || '/app') %>">Continue with Discord</a>
        <a class="back-home" href="/">← Back to Chirpy</a>
      </section>
    </main>

  <% } else if (page === "onboarding") { %>
    <main class="auth-page">
      <a class="auth-brand" href="/"><img src="/images/chirpy.png?v=1" alt="" /> CHIRPY</a>
      <section class="auth-card">
        <div class="auth-logo"><img src="/images/chirpy.png?v=1" alt="Chirpy" /></div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Make it yours</p>
        <h1>Set up your profile</h1>
        <p>Choose the name and handle people will see when you join the conversation.</p>
